{"id": "3.3-00265", "case_id": "t3.5.s1p.0e9cb5725f57d9bf1015.rhs_4a727ff75ec5bb20", "parent_id": "t1.3.s1p.0e9cb5725f57d9bf1015", "source": null, "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Round-trip: Stage 1 → generated text → Stage 2</h2><div class=\"stage-grid\"><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 1</div><h3>Write the whole-module specification</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>Clean module RTL: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>stage1/design.v</a></td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Describe the interface, parameters, and observable behavior of this clean design. Return a self-contained specification, not RTL implementation code. A separate isolated call will receive your specification.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=stage1%2FTASK.md'>stage1/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Generated whole-module specification (prose).</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage1/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=stage1%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module mg_05943 (inout wire pad,input wire oe,input wire op);\nassign pad = oe ? op : 1&#x27;bz; \n endmodule</pre></details></div><div class='card'><div class='stage-step'>STAGE 2</div><h3>Repair the module</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Input</th><td>The generated Stage 1 text plus buggy mutant rtl: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>stage2_template/design.v</a>. Required top module: mg_05943.</td></tr><tr><th>Instruction</th><td>Repair the functional fault in design.v using the specification and retained RTL context. Return the complete corrected RTL with the same top module. Only the default configuration is scored.<p class='muted small'>Stored wording: <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=stage2_template%2FTASK.md'>stage2_template/TASK.md</a></p></td></tr><tr><th>Output</th><td><strong>Complete repaired RTL module.</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><details><summary>Read input: stage2_template/design.v · <a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=stage2_template%2Fdesign.v'>Open raw</a></summary><pre>module mg_05943 (inout wire pad,input wire oe,input wire op);\nassign pad = ~(oe ? op : 1&#x27;bz); \n endmodule</pre></details></div></div><div class=\"flow\"><strong>Stage 1 output → abstraction gate → fresh Stage 2 input.</strong> The intermediate text is generated separately for each model/attempt. It is not a prefilled golden description. Stage 2 receives neither the clean RTL nor the Stage 1 conversation.</div><h2>Private final evaluation</h2><div class=\"card\"><table><tbody><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Reference RTL</th><td><a href='#task=3.3&amp;case=3.3-00265&amp;file=private%2Fgolden.v'>private/golden.v</a></td></tr><tr><th style=\"width:175px\">Score / oracle</th><td>Binary formal equivalence to the hidden clean module</td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"muted\">The formal oracle consumes the complete Stage 2 RTL file and compares it with the clean reference. A golden RTL file is scoring material, not a generated Stage 1 output.</p></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/450dea840c7258fd7bcf293e3434c6ec3de797480ff585991fc31f2e70dc2d0c.txt", "size": 4487, "binary": false, "section": "Other: case.json"}, {"name": "private/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/268328c41ff051297a3754437be56de9cfd48359db165df0e3d17a03e1b6fa51.txt", "size": 595, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/golden.v", "url": "assets/0e9cb5725f57d9bf1015abb75254e74d3a1b872468d950ae1a02a5ae99d2bab2.txt", "size": 102, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification/negative/equivalence.ys", "url": "assets/268328c41ff051297a3754437be56de9cfd48359db165df0e3d17a03e1b6fa51.txt", "size": 595, "binary": false, "section": "Private reference and oracle"}, {"name": "private/qualification